1
00:00:01,376 --> 00:00:04,003
You said
you'd marry Joey?

2
00:00:04,045 --> 00:00:06,381
You have to realize
I was exhausted

3
00:00:06,423 --> 00:00:07,716
I was emotional...

4
00:00:07,758 --> 00:00:09,551
I would have said yes
to anybody.

5
00:00:09,593 --> 00:00:11,762
Like the time
when you and I got married.

6
00:00:13,848 --> 00:00:16,642
I'm not helping.

7
00:00:16,684 --> 00:00:18,727
So you said
yes to him

8
00:00:18,769 --> 00:00:21,396
and you just had
our baby.

9
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:23,315
That is right.

10
00:00:23,357 --> 00:00:26,193
And traditionally,
the daddy is supposed
to give the mommy a present

11
00:00:26,234 --> 00:00:27,945
but I am prepared
to let that go.

12
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:30,865
So when I came in here

13
00:00:30,906 --> 00:00:33,408
to see if you wanted to maybe
start things up again

14
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:36,411
you were engaged
to my best friend.

15
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:39,957
Well... really?

16
00:00:39,999 --> 00:00:41,876
I thought Chandler
was your best friend.

17
00:00:41,917 --> 00:00:44,962
Chandler's my oldest friend.

18
00:00:45,004 --> 00:00:46,296
Joey's more... No. uh-uh-uh!

19
00:00:48,256 --> 00:00:49,758
Hey, guys, I'm
gonna take off.

20
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,426
I just wanted
to say good-bye.

21
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:53,470
Rachel said she'd marry you?

22
00:00:54,805 --> 00:00:57,349
This isn't the right room.
Sorry, folks.

23
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:07,484
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

24
00:01:07,526 --> 00:01:09,778
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

25
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:13,032
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

26
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:17,786
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

27
00:01:17,828 --> 00:01:20,497
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

28
00:01:20,539 --> 00:01:23,667
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

29
00:01:23,709 --> 00:01:27,755
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

30
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:30,173
♪ When the rain starts to pour ♪

31
00:01:30,215 --> 00:01:32,634
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

32
00:01:32,676 --> 00:01:35,178
♪ Like I've been there before ♪

33
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:37,681
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

34
00:01:37,723 --> 00:01:41,518
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

35
00:01:50,819 --> 00:01:52,947
Okay, I don't
want to be negative

36
00:01:52,988 --> 00:01:55,532
so I'll say that most
of the signs you bought
are good.

37
00:01:57,826 --> 00:01:59,912
No, they ran out
of "It's a girl."

38
00:01:59,954 --> 00:02:01,956
But I can fix this one.

39
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:08,253
You see?

40
00:02:08,295 --> 00:02:10,130
Mm-hmm.

41
00:02:11,757 --> 00:02:13,717
So sexy.

42
00:02:13,759 --> 00:02:15,427
Honey?

43
00:02:15,469 --> 00:02:17,805
Yeah?

44
00:02:18,931 --> 00:02:21,058
Honey, why don't you go
lie down?

45
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:23,268
No, no, it's okay-- Ross
and Rachel will be back soon

46
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:24,770
and then I got to go
to the office.

47
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:31,150
Am I producing them?

48
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:33,737
Why are you so tired?

49
00:02:33,779 --> 00:02:35,072
I couldn't sleep last night.

50
00:02:35,114 --> 00:02:36,782
And then I start worrying

51
00:02:36,824 --> 00:02:38,700
about this big divisional
meeting I have later today.

52
00:02:38,742 --> 00:02:41,244
The more I worried about it,
the more I couldn't sleep.

53
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:42,788
You know, I was like

54
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:45,248
"If I fall asleep now,
I'll get six hours' sleep."

55
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:48,585
Then, "If I fall asleep now,
I'll get five hours' sleep."

56
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:50,796
No matter what I did,
I couldn't fall asleep.

57
00:02:50,838 --> 00:02:52,422
You know what
you should have done?

58
00:02:52,464 --> 00:02:54,633
You should have told yourself
that little story.

59
00:02:56,969 --> 00:02:58,428
Hi.

60
00:02:58,470 --> 00:03:00,014
Welcome home.

61
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:01,556
Phoebe did the signs.

62
00:03:02,683 --> 00:03:03,809
RACHEL:
Oh, you guys.

63
00:03:03,851 --> 00:03:06,311
Thanks for
doing this.

64
00:03:06,353 --> 00:03:07,604
Look at all stuff
people sent.

65
00:03:07,646 --> 00:03:09,356
Ohh... ah!

66
00:03:09,397 --> 00:03:12,275
Oh, my gosh. Look, there's
something every mother needs.

67
00:03:12,317 --> 00:03:14,444
A giant stuffed gorilla

68
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:17,614
that takes up
the entire apartment.

69
00:03:17,656 --> 00:03:19,658
What are people think...

70
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:22,870
Oh, you guys, I love it.

71
00:03:23,871 --> 00:03:26,040
And so, where's Ross?

72
00:03:26,081 --> 00:03:28,583
He's downstairs
getting the stuff
out of the cab.

73
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:30,377
Uh, is he still mad at us?

74
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:31,545
Well, you more than me.

75
00:03:31,586 --> 00:03:33,130
But he can't stay too mad at me.

76
00:03:33,172 --> 00:03:34,589
I mean, I just had his baby.

77
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:37,759
That's not fair.
I can't do that.

78
00:03:37,801 --> 00:03:40,220
Yeah, and I'm not so sure you
should be here when he comes up.

79
00:03:40,261 --> 00:03:41,513
See, this is
what I was afraid of.

80
00:03:41,555 --> 00:03:42,973
I didn't think
I should be here either

81
00:03:43,015 --> 00:03:44,516
but somebody said
he'd be over it by now.

82
00:03:44,558 --> 00:03:45,726
Hey, what do I know?

83
00:03:45,767 --> 00:03:47,310
I wanted to get
a bigger gorilla.

84
00:03:53,483 --> 00:03:54,693
The numbers
we're seeing

85
00:03:54,735 --> 00:03:56,361
in Chicago, New York
and London

86
00:03:56,403 --> 00:03:57,571
are consistently solid

87
00:03:57,612 --> 00:03:59,073
but many of our
field offices

88
00:03:59,114 --> 00:04:01,033
have reported
disappointing yields.

89
00:04:07,873 --> 00:04:09,833
Boston is down,
Atlanta is down

90
00:04:09,875 --> 00:04:12,419
Houston is down--
I could go on and on

91
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,088
but instead
of boring you

92
00:04:14,129 --> 00:04:17,549
I'll go straight
to my 42-point plan.

93
00:04:27,184 --> 00:04:28,518
Walter.

94
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:32,981
PHOEBE:
She's just so cute.

95
00:04:33,023 --> 00:04:35,525
Oh, I just want
to bite her ear off

96
00:04:35,567 --> 00:04:37,736
and use it
as a sucking candy.

97
00:04:39,113 --> 00:04:40,321
Phoebe!

98
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:42,866
But I could take one
of those little feet

99
00:04:42,908 --> 00:04:44,743
and put it
in a pita pocket.

100
00:04:46,036 --> 00:04:48,122
Okay, I put most
of the stuff away.

101
00:04:48,163 --> 00:04:49,497
Oh, great. The pacifiers?

102
00:04:49,539 --> 00:04:51,166
Uh, it's in
the cupboard.

103
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:52,375
The burping cloths?

104
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:53,710
Uh, linen closet.

105
00:04:53,752 --> 00:04:55,336
The diapers?

106
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:56,964
In the hospital.

107
00:04:58,506 --> 00:05:00,550
You guys got
a hospital? Fancy.

108
00:05:02,261 --> 00:05:04,221
Well, I, uh, left
the diapers at
the hospital.

109
00:05:04,263 --> 00:05:06,389
There's some in the
bag, but I'll run out
and get some more.

110
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:08,100
All right, thanks.

111
00:05:08,142 --> 00:05:10,351
Could you stop at the coffee
house and get me a muffin?

112
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:12,104
Oh, sure. What kind?

113
00:05:12,146 --> 00:05:13,563
Uh, let me think.

114
00:05:13,605 --> 00:05:14,940
What do I want?

115
00:05:17,067 --> 00:05:19,611
What do I want?

116
00:05:19,653 --> 00:05:20,862
Please, take your time.

117
00:05:20,904 --> 00:05:22,572
It's an important decision.

118
00:05:22,614 --> 00:05:24,908
Not like, say, I don't know,
deciding to marry someone.

119
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:27,953
This is about a muffin.

120
00:05:30,622 --> 00:05:31,581
Blueberry.

121
00:05:31,623 --> 00:05:34,251
Blueberry it is.
Thank you.

122
00:05:35,502 --> 00:05:37,629
Wow, he's really not
letting this go, is he?

123
00:05:37,671 --> 00:05:40,132
How long do you think
that's going to last?

124
00:05:40,174 --> 00:05:41,800
Well, I don't know--
he got over

125
00:05:41,842 --> 00:05:44,261
the "we were on a break" thing
really quickly.

126
00:05:44,303 --> 00:05:48,765
You know, I can't even
worry about it right now.

127
00:05:48,807 --> 00:05:51,518
'Cause I've got
the cutie little baby.

128
00:05:51,559 --> 00:05:54,813
Oh, I can't believe
how much I love her.

129
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:56,690
I mean, I can't get enough
of her.

130
00:05:56,731 --> 00:05:58,275
Like, right now, I miss her.

131
00:05:58,317 --> 00:05:59,442
I actually miss her.

132
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:02,654
You know, that's... that's her.

133
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:07,617
Oh, God, look
at her sleeping.

134
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:09,786
Oh, I love you so much.

135
00:06:09,828 --> 00:06:11,746
I think I'm going
to wake her up.

136
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:13,832
No, no, Rach. You know,
you're never supposed

137
00:06:13,874 --> 00:06:15,083
to wake a sleeping baby.

138
00:06:15,125 --> 00:06:16,543
I can do whatever I want.

139
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:17,669
I made her.

140
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:21,715
Come on, little
girl, oh, yes.

141
00:06:21,756 --> 00:06:24,134
Hello, Emma, hi.

142
00:06:24,176 --> 00:06:25,135
( Emma crying )

143
00:06:25,177 --> 00:06:27,221
Oh...

144
00:06:27,262 --> 00:06:28,847
Oh, I'm sorry.

145
00:06:28,889 --> 00:06:30,682
I would say "I told you so"

146
00:06:30,724 --> 00:06:33,060
but she's kind of doing that
for me.

147
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:34,519
I'm sorry.

148
00:06:34,561 --> 00:06:35,770
Oh, Mommy's so sorry.

149
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:37,022
Go back to sleep...
shh-shh-shh.

150
00:06:37,064 --> 00:06:39,024
Go back to sleep.

151
00:06:39,066 --> 00:06:41,235
It really breaks
your heart, doesn't it?

152
00:06:41,276 --> 00:06:42,944
It really does.

153
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:47,241
How long do you think
we have to stay?

154
00:06:48,867 --> 00:06:52,120
Okay, if everyone's on board,
it's settled. Chandler!

155
00:06:59,753 --> 00:07:00,461
Chandler!

156
00:07:00,503 --> 00:07:01,462
Yeah?

157
00:07:01,504 --> 00:07:02,923
Are you
on board?

158
00:07:04,299 --> 00:07:06,593
Yes.

159
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:08,095
Then problem solved.

160
00:07:08,136 --> 00:07:10,264
Chandler will be running
our office in Tulsa.

161
00:07:10,305 --> 00:07:12,391
You're going
to love Oklahoma.

162
00:07:14,684 --> 00:07:16,186
( Emma crying )

163
00:07:16,228 --> 00:07:17,854
All right,
we already tried

164
00:07:17,896 --> 00:07:20,440
feeding her,
changing her,
burping her...

165
00:07:20,481 --> 00:07:21,691
Oh, try this one.

166
00:07:21,733 --> 00:07:24,736
Go back in time
and listen to Phoebe.

167
00:07:26,738 --> 00:07:28,615
All right, here's something.

168
00:07:28,656 --> 00:07:31,952
It says to try holding the baby
close to your body

169
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:34,329
and then swing her rapidly
from side to side.

170
00:07:34,371 --> 00:07:35,789
Okay.

171
00:07:43,213 --> 00:07:44,839
( crying stops )

172
00:07:44,881 --> 00:07:46,507
It worked.

173
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:51,763
Oh... no... just stopped
to throw up a little bit.

174
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:55,225
Oh, what am I going to do?

175
00:07:55,267 --> 00:07:58,561
It's been hours
and it won't stop crying.

176
00:07:58,603 --> 00:08:00,397
Uh, "she," Rach.

177
00:08:00,439 --> 00:08:01,564
Not "it"-- "she."

178
00:08:01,606 --> 00:08:04,067
Yeah, I'm not so sure.

179
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:07,112
God, I'm losing
my mind.

180
00:08:07,154 --> 00:08:08,238
Yeah, no kidding.

181
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:10,407
This just proves
no good can come

182
00:08:10,449 --> 00:08:12,242
from having sex with Ross!

183
00:08:17,456 --> 00:08:21,335
Hey, Gunther,
could I get a couple of
blueberry muffins to go?

184
00:08:21,376 --> 00:08:23,003
Diapers, huh?

185
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:24,087
Yep.

186
00:08:24,129 --> 00:08:25,713
So I guess Rachel
had your baby.

187
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:28,133
Yep. Can you believe it?

188
00:08:28,175 --> 00:08:30,135
Nope.

189
00:08:30,177 --> 00:08:33,512
I can't even believe she slept
with you in the first place.

190
00:08:33,554 --> 00:08:35,098
Huh?

191
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:39,436
Oh, oh, you mean like, uh...

192
00:08:39,478 --> 00:08:40,770
Huh?

193
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:46,567
Hey.

194
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:49,154
Your muffins.

195
00:08:49,196 --> 00:08:50,947
Ross, I know
you're pissed at me

196
00:08:50,989 --> 00:08:52,657
but we have to talk
about this.

197
00:08:52,699 --> 00:08:55,243
Uh, actually, uh,
we don't.

198
00:08:55,285 --> 00:08:57,287
Fine, okay, fine,
but I got to say

199
00:08:57,329 --> 00:08:59,998
technically, I didn't
even do anything wrong.

200
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:04,711
What? You didn't
do anything wrong?

201
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:08,548
I-I said I didn't technically.

202
00:09:08,589 --> 00:09:10,675
Well, let's put aside
the fact that you

203
00:09:10,717 --> 00:09:13,220
"accidentally" picked up
my grandmother's ring

204
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:15,514
and you "accidentally"
proposed to Rachel...

205
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:17,891
Can I just stop you
right there for a second?

206
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:19,518
When people do this...

207
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:22,187
I don't really know
what that means.

208
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:29,110
You were saying?

209
00:09:29,152 --> 00:09:32,531
And I can even
understand that you
couldn't tell Rachel

210
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:34,657
but why couldn't
you tell me, huh?

211
00:09:34,699 --> 00:09:38,036
You had all day to,
and you didn't.

212
00:09:38,078 --> 00:09:40,247
I know. I should have.

213
00:09:40,288 --> 00:09:41,498
I'm "sorry."

214
00:09:45,752 --> 00:09:48,838
Not using it right, Joe.

215
00:09:53,634 --> 00:09:56,179
I'm going to go.

216
00:09:56,221 --> 00:09:57,431
No. Come on, look, Ross.

217
00:09:57,472 --> 00:09:58,723
We have to get past this.

218
00:09:58,765 --> 00:09:59,807
Give me the bag.

219
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:01,142
No. I don't know
what else to do.

220
00:10:01,184 --> 00:10:02,143
I said I'm sorry.

221
00:10:02,185 --> 00:10:03,478
Joey...

222
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:04,729
Now you should
scream at me

223
00:10:04,771 --> 00:10:05,813
or curse me or hit me.

224
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:07,023
I'm not going
to hit you.

225
00:10:07,065 --> 00:10:08,400
Why not?

226
00:10:08,442 --> 00:10:09,526
You'll feel better.
I'll feel better.

227
00:10:09,568 --> 00:10:10,527
And you know
you want to.

228
00:10:10,569 --> 00:10:11,611
I can see it in your eyes.

229
00:10:11,652 --> 00:10:12,695
No, I don't.

230
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:13,947
A little bit.

231
00:10:13,988 --> 00:10:14,989
No.

232
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:16,199
A little bit.

233
00:10:16,241 --> 00:10:17,700
No.

234
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:19,453
A little bit more.

235
00:10:19,494 --> 00:10:20,995
Give me the bag.
No, hit me.

236
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:22,330
Give me the bag.
Hit me.

237
00:10:22,372 --> 00:10:24,040
Joey, give me the bag.
Hit me. Hit me.

238
00:10:24,082 --> 00:10:26,209
Joe, I'm not kidding.
Hit me! Hit me! Hit me!

239
00:10:38,597 --> 00:10:40,681
You ducked!

240
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:42,476
I'm sorry. It was a reflex.

241
00:10:42,517 --> 00:10:43,477
Oh, my God!

242
00:10:43,518 --> 00:10:44,644
This really hurts!

243
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:46,104
I couldn't help it.

244
00:10:46,146 --> 00:10:48,356
When a fist comes
at your face, you duck.

245
00:10:48,398 --> 00:10:49,441
Look.

246
00:10:52,110 --> 00:10:54,779
What is the matter with you?!

247
00:10:54,821 --> 00:10:57,031
You were supposed to duck.
Why didn't you duck?

248
00:10:57,073 --> 00:10:59,242
Why don't we talk about this
on the way to the hospital.

249
00:10:59,284 --> 00:11:00,785
Good, good, yeah.

250
00:11:00,827 --> 00:11:03,704
Maybe while we're there,
they can check your reflexes.

251
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,418
"Oops."

252
00:11:15,967 --> 00:11:19,053
( Emma crying )

253
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:20,597
Try feeding her again.

254
00:11:20,639 --> 00:11:22,599
I already fed her.

255
00:11:22,641 --> 00:11:25,435
I know.
That's why I said "again."

256
00:11:27,521 --> 00:11:29,481
You guys, we can't turn
on each other, okay?

257
00:11:29,523 --> 00:11:31,274
That's just what she wants.

258
00:11:31,316 --> 00:11:32,984
Hi.
MONICA:
Hey.

259
00:11:33,026 --> 00:11:34,819
Monica, can I talk
to you outside
for a minute?

260
00:11:34,861 --> 00:11:36,154
Oh, no, you guys
just stay here.

261
00:11:36,196 --> 00:11:37,489
I'm going to go
check her diaper.

262
00:11:37,531 --> 00:11:38,573
Pheebs, you want to come?

263
00:11:38,615 --> 00:11:41,660
Oh, I'm kind of
part of this.

264
00:11:43,036 --> 00:11:44,371
Actually, Pheebs

265
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:46,289
it's more of a husband and wife
kind of thing.

266
00:11:46,331 --> 00:11:48,958
I knew I should have
married Chandler.

267
00:11:50,627 --> 00:11:51,919
Okay, what's up?

268
00:11:51,961 --> 00:11:53,380
Okay, um...

269
00:11:53,421 --> 00:11:55,131
You know how we always
said it would be fun

270
00:11:55,173 --> 00:11:56,633
to move to Paris
for a year?

271
00:11:56,675 --> 00:11:58,009
You could study
French cooking

272
00:11:58,051 --> 00:12:00,679
and I could write,
and we could picnic

273
00:12:00,719 --> 00:12:01,762
along the Seine

274
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:03,557
and go wine tasting
in Bordeaux?

275
00:12:03,598 --> 00:12:05,099
Oh, yes.

276
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:10,855
Okay, you know how
people say that Tulsa...

277
00:12:10,897 --> 00:12:13,274
is the Paris of Oklahoma?

278
00:12:13,316 --> 00:12:17,362
What? Who says that?

279
00:12:17,404 --> 00:12:21,074
People who have
never been to Paris.

280
00:12:21,115 --> 00:12:23,034
Wh-What's going on?

281
00:12:23,076 --> 00:12:26,413
We're moving to Tulsa.

282
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:29,832
Excuse me?

283
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:31,876
Okay, Ms. McKenna

284
00:12:31,918 --> 00:12:34,045
she kind of, uh,
works above my boss.

285
00:12:34,087 --> 00:12:35,589
She asked me
to move to Tulsa

286
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:37,382
and be the president
of our office there

287
00:12:37,424 --> 00:12:40,885
and I was sleeping and
apparently said yes.

288
00:12:40,927 --> 00:12:42,887
Tulsa, Oklahoma?!

289
00:12:42,929 --> 00:12:44,681
The Sooner state.

290
00:12:46,015 --> 00:12:47,975
Whatever that is.

291
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:51,563
Chandler, I don't even want
to see the musical Oklahoma!

292
00:12:51,605 --> 00:12:53,231
Really? "Oh, What
a Beautiful Morning"?

293
00:12:53,273 --> 00:12:54,815
"Surrey With
The Fringe On Top"?

294
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:57,736
Are you trying to tell me
that we're moving to Oklahoma

295
00:12:57,776 --> 00:13:00,071
or that you're gay?

296
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:02,073
Not that this matters

297
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:04,701
but did they at least
offer you a huge raise?

298
00:13:04,743 --> 00:13:06,202
No, no.

299
00:13:06,244 --> 00:13:09,163
But they are going to
lease us a Ford Focus.

300
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:11,958
I'll get out of it.

301
00:13:11,999 --> 00:13:12,959
Thank you.

302
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,168
( Emma crying )

303
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:15,378
What is wrong with Emma?

304
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:16,795
Oh, she misunderstood.

305
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:18,632
She thought she
was moving to Tulsa.

306
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:26,306
Ma'am, do you
have a minute?

307
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:28,266
I kind of have some bad news.

308
00:13:28,308 --> 00:13:30,393
I don't think
I can move to Tulsa.

309
00:13:30,435 --> 00:13:32,103
What?

310
00:13:32,145 --> 00:13:34,606
Uh, it's a funny story,
actually.

311
00:13:34,648 --> 00:13:36,399
( clears throat )

312
00:13:36,441 --> 00:13:40,069
Uh, I kind of fell asleep
in the meeting this morning.

313
00:13:40,111 --> 00:13:41,613
So when I said
I'd move to Tulsa

314
00:13:41,655 --> 00:13:43,406
I didn't really know
what I was saying.

315
00:13:43,448 --> 00:13:44,783
You fell asleep?

316
00:13:44,823 --> 00:13:46,284
But only because
I was up all night

317
00:13:46,326 --> 00:13:47,577
worried about this meeting.

318
00:13:47,619 --> 00:13:49,245
Isn't that funny?

319
00:13:50,913 --> 00:13:53,708
Irony. Not a fan?
All right.

320
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:57,044
See, here's the thing.

321
00:13:57,086 --> 00:14:00,632
I went home and told my wife
about Tulsa, a-and she won't go.

322
00:14:00,674 --> 00:14:02,550
See, me? I love Tulsa.

323
00:14:02,592 --> 00:14:04,469
Tulsa is heaven.
Tulsa is Italy.

324
00:14:04,511 --> 00:14:06,971
Please don't make me go there.

325
00:14:07,013 --> 00:14:08,682
Chandler, I...
No, now, now

326
00:14:08,723 --> 00:14:11,476
look, Carol...
Can I call you Carol?

327
00:14:13,186 --> 00:14:15,814
Why would I
when your name is Elaine?

328
00:14:18,525 --> 00:14:23,697
Oh, what a great picture
of your son. Strapping!

329
00:14:25,114 --> 00:14:28,660
That's a picture
of your daughter, isn't it?

330
00:14:28,702 --> 00:14:30,077
Well, she's lovely.

331
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:32,706
I-I like a girl
with a strong jaw.

332
00:14:35,166 --> 00:14:36,668
I'll call you from Tulsa.

333
00:14:41,214 --> 00:14:43,842
Hey. So, uh, how is it?

334
00:14:43,882 --> 00:14:46,427
I broke my thumb.

335
00:14:46,469 --> 00:14:48,513
Your thumb?

336
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:52,475
That's weird.

337
00:14:52,517 --> 00:14:54,060
Are you sure you're
punching right?

338
00:14:54,101 --> 00:14:55,269
Make a fist.

339
00:14:56,813 --> 00:14:59,524
Maybe later.

340
00:14:59,566 --> 00:15:01,401
Ross, I feel terrible.

341
00:15:01,442 --> 00:15:02,610
You know what, you can go.

342
00:15:02,652 --> 00:15:05,697
I just have
to fill out some forms.

343
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:12,579
You, uh, y-you want me
to help you with that?

344
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:14,372
Why, does it look
like I'm having trouble

345
00:15:14,414 --> 00:15:16,583
with my misshapen claw?

346
00:15:19,085 --> 00:15:21,838
"Name."

347
00:15:23,506 --> 00:15:26,384
I know "Ross," but
what's it short for?

348
00:15:26,426 --> 00:15:28,678
You know, like, Rossell.

349
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:33,099
Or Rosstopher.

350
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:34,392
Just Ross.

351
00:15:34,434 --> 00:15:35,769
Oh.

352
00:15:35,810 --> 00:15:37,478
It's pretty.

353
00:15:39,146 --> 00:15:40,815
Okay, "Date of birth."

354
00:15:40,857 --> 00:15:42,275
You know my birthday.

355
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:45,152
Sure.

356
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:46,987
May...

357
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:49,407
tember?

358
00:15:49,449 --> 00:15:51,950
October 18th.

359
00:15:51,992 --> 00:15:54,913
"Occupation."
Dinosaurs.

360
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:59,125
Actually, I'm a paleo...

361
00:15:59,166 --> 00:16:02,420
Dinosaurs is fine.

362
00:16:02,462 --> 00:16:04,004
The drawing is not.

363
00:16:08,593 --> 00:16:12,012
All right, uh,
w-who do you want as
your emergency contact?

364
00:16:12,054 --> 00:16:14,223
Uh, Rachel, I guess.

365
00:16:14,265 --> 00:16:16,350
Okay. "Relationship"?

366
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:18,060
Whoo, boy, this
could take a while.

367
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:23,691
Just, uh...
just put "roommate."

368
00:16:23,733 --> 00:16:24,859
Come on.

369
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:26,360
You guys are
more than that.

370
00:16:26,402 --> 00:16:28,404
I mean, you're going
to get together, right?

371
00:16:28,446 --> 00:16:30,615
I don't think that we are.

372
00:16:30,657 --> 00:16:34,869
But... you two are
supposed to be together.

373
00:16:34,911 --> 00:16:36,287
Well, I thought so, too

374
00:16:36,329 --> 00:16:38,289
but then she said
she'd marry you.

375
00:16:38,331 --> 00:16:40,374
Come on, Ross, that
didn't mean anything.

376
00:16:40,416 --> 00:16:42,251
She-she'd just had the baby.

377
00:16:42,293 --> 00:16:44,420
She was all freaked out
about doing it alone.

378
00:16:44,462 --> 00:16:46,339
Sh-She would have
said yes to anybody.

379
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:48,382
Yeah, th-that's what she said.

380
00:16:48,424 --> 00:16:49,550
So?

381
00:16:49,592 --> 00:16:51,761
So, I don't want
to be just anybody.

382
00:16:53,847 --> 00:16:55,932
Wow.

383
00:16:55,974 --> 00:16:57,016
You know what?

384
00:16:57,057 --> 00:16:59,769
It's-it's better
this way anyway.

385
00:16:59,811 --> 00:17:02,313
I mean, I don't know
what I was thinking

386
00:17:02,355 --> 00:17:04,231
going down that road
again with us.

387
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:06,860
It's just much easier
if we're...

388
00:17:06,901 --> 00:17:09,821
if we're just friends
who have a kid.

389
00:17:09,863 --> 00:17:11,447
Really?
Yeah.

390
00:17:11,489 --> 00:17:13,616
A-And you're okay with that?

391
00:17:13,658 --> 00:17:15,910
Yes. I mean, it's what
we always planned.

392
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:18,830
And if you have a plan,
you should stick to it.

393
00:17:18,872 --> 00:17:22,291
That's-that's why they
call them "plans." Hello?

394
00:17:24,544 --> 00:17:26,629
I'm fine.

395
00:17:26,671 --> 00:17:29,340
Hey, for what it's worth

396
00:17:29,382 --> 00:17:33,970
with Rachel, I don't
think you'll ever be
just "anybody."

397
00:17:34,012 --> 00:17:36,055
Hey, there you go.

398
00:17:38,224 --> 00:17:39,350
"Thanks."

399
00:17:42,562 --> 00:17:45,857
( Emma crying )

400
00:17:45,899 --> 00:17:49,402
Oh, my God.
How long has she been crying?

401
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:51,905
About a week
and a half.

402
00:17:51,946 --> 00:17:54,323
Well, it looks like
you guys got it under control

403
00:17:54,365 --> 00:17:55,575
so I'm just going to go.

404
00:17:57,911 --> 00:17:59,370
No? Really?

405
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:02,122
Misery really does love company?
All right.

406
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:06,502
Try holding her
a different way.

407
00:18:06,544 --> 00:18:08,421
Look, you guys,
I'm doing the best I can.

408
00:18:08,462 --> 00:18:10,506
Anyone else is welcome to try.

409
00:18:10,548 --> 00:18:11,883
All right, I'll try.
Fine. Yes.

410
00:18:11,925 --> 00:18:13,009
Okay.
Okay.

411
00:18:13,051 --> 00:18:14,052
Here you go.

412
00:18:14,092 --> 00:18:15,386
Oh, gosh.

413
00:18:15,428 --> 00:18:17,096
Shh...
( crying stops )

414
00:18:17,137 --> 00:18:19,390
Nothing works with this child!
( crying starts again )

415
00:18:19,432 --> 00:18:22,518
Oh, God, what am I going
to do, you guys?

416
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:24,437
I can't even comfort
my own baby.

417
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:25,813
I'm the worst mother ever.

418
00:18:25,855 --> 00:18:27,356
No, you're just new at this.

419
00:18:27,398 --> 00:18:29,067
You'll get better.

420
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:30,860
Think about
your first day at work.

421
00:18:30,902 --> 00:18:33,237
That couldn't have been easy,
but you figured that out.

422
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:35,406
Yeah, I don't think
dressing provocatively

423
00:18:35,448 --> 00:18:38,076
is going to help me here.

424
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:39,953
( sighs ):
Oh, God. Just please take her.

425
00:18:39,994 --> 00:18:43,081
Okay, I'll take her.

426
00:18:43,121 --> 00:18:45,458
I have to go
to the bathroom.

427
00:18:45,499 --> 00:18:47,334
I have to go scream
into a pillow.

428
00:18:51,631 --> 00:18:53,299
Bouncy...

429
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:54,759
♪ Bouncy baby ♪

430
00:18:54,801 --> 00:18:56,552
♪ Bouncy baby ♪

431
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:59,305
♪ Oh, baby, baby... ♪

432
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:01,557
♪ Oh, baby, baby... ♪

433
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:04,644
♪ Oh, baby, baby... ♪
( crying stops )

434
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:09,398
Have I gone deaf?

435
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:12,485
It worked.

436
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:14,904
♪ Oh, baby, baby, baby... ♪

437
00:19:14,946 --> 00:19:16,948
♪ Oh, baby, baby,
baby... ♪

438
00:19:16,990 --> 00:19:19,784
You must be a fireball in bed.

439
00:19:21,035 --> 00:19:23,037
( whispers ):
I can't believe it.

440
00:19:23,079 --> 00:19:24,455
She's asleep.

441
00:19:24,497 --> 00:19:26,874
I got her to go to sleep.

442
00:19:26,916 --> 00:19:29,836
I have actual magical powers.

443
00:19:31,671 --> 00:19:34,548
I can hear traffic and birds.

444
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:37,093
I can hear the voices
in my head again.

445
00:19:38,761 --> 00:19:40,596
I'm kidding.

446
00:19:43,599 --> 00:19:45,643
Oh, my God.

447
00:19:45,685 --> 00:19:47,979
You got her to stop crying.

448
00:19:48,021 --> 00:19:49,438
Yes, I did.

449
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:52,316
I'm Monica, Super Aunt.

450
00:19:52,358 --> 00:19:56,029
You are the official
baby-crier-stopper.

451
00:19:56,070 --> 00:19:57,404
Yes, I am.

452
00:19:57,446 --> 00:19:59,239
You're never leaving
the apartment.

453
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:01,117
Say what?

454
00:20:01,159 --> 00:20:02,660
That's your new job.

455
00:20:02,702 --> 00:20:05,663
Day or night, she starts crying,
I need you here.

456
00:20:05,705 --> 00:20:06,873
Oh, no, no, no.

457
00:20:06,914 --> 00:20:09,207
All right,
well, uh, thankfully

458
00:20:09,249 --> 00:20:11,669
you don't need me
at all, so...

459
00:20:11,711 --> 00:20:13,713
Hey, Super Aunt, see you later.

460
00:20:13,754 --> 00:20:17,675
Rachel, let's give it
six to eight months.

461
00:20:26,392 --> 00:20:29,269
Okay, so listen,
I'm going to go lay down.

462
00:20:29,311 --> 00:20:31,230
What?

463
00:20:31,271 --> 00:20:33,482
You know, the book says
that whenever she's sleeping

464
00:20:33,524 --> 00:20:36,276
I should be sleeping.
So... oh...

465
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:43,283
Hey.

466
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:46,204
Shh! We just got her
to go to sleep.

467
00:20:46,245 --> 00:20:48,873
Oh, so th-there can't be
any yelling?

468
00:20:48,915 --> 00:20:51,792
No.

469
00:20:54,921 --> 00:20:56,923
We're moving to Tulsa.

470
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:58,091
What?!
Shh!

471
00:20:58,132 --> 00:20:59,550
Shh!

472
00:20:59,592 --> 00:21:01,928
Shh!

473
00:21:01,969 --> 00:21:03,888
I can't... I can't hear.

474
00:21:08,768 --> 00:21:11,520
Hey.

475
00:21:11,562 --> 00:21:13,189
Hey.

476
00:21:13,231 --> 00:21:14,899
Where have you been?

477
00:21:14,941 --> 00:21:16,901
( gasps )

478
00:21:16,943 --> 00:21:18,569
What happened to you?

479
00:21:18,611 --> 00:21:20,362
I had a little
thing with Joey.

480
00:21:20,404 --> 00:21:22,823
If you think this is bad,
you should see him.

481
00:21:22,865 --> 00:21:26,827
No, Ross, this is not good.

482
00:21:26,869 --> 00:21:29,080
Please, we have to talk
about this Joey thing.

483
00:21:29,122 --> 00:21:30,164
Please sit.

484
00:21:34,252 --> 00:21:38,047
All right, you have got
to get over this Joey thing.

485
00:21:38,089 --> 00:21:43,594
Okay, I never really wanted
to marry Joey, okay?

486
00:21:43,636 --> 00:21:46,597
Okay.

487
00:21:46,639 --> 00:21:51,102
You know what I really,
really want?

488
00:21:51,144 --> 00:21:55,648
What, Rach?

489
00:21:55,689 --> 00:21:59,568
I want to sleep.

490
00:21:59,610 --> 00:22:02,280
I want to eat.

491
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:05,365
I want to take a shower.

492
00:22:05,407 --> 00:22:06,826
I mean,
before she wakes up

493
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:08,661
and we got to do this
all over again.

494
00:22:08,702 --> 00:22:11,413
Right.

495
00:22:11,455 --> 00:22:13,291
I mean, 'cause I got
news for you, mister.

496
00:22:13,331 --> 00:22:16,502
Emma? Not easy.

497
00:22:16,543 --> 00:22:21,132
Well... that's
what I'm here for.

498
00:22:21,174 --> 00:22:23,801
( Emma crying )

499
00:22:23,843 --> 00:22:25,594
Want me to get that?

500
00:22:25,636 --> 00:22:27,513
No, that's really okay.

501
00:22:27,554 --> 00:22:28,681
Monica!

502
00:22:28,722 --> 00:22:30,224
I got it, got it, got it.

503
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:43,487
You know, uh,
I've been thinking about this

504
00:22:43,529 --> 00:22:45,489
and I got to tell you,
it's not my fault.

505
00:22:45,531 --> 00:22:46,782
It's a natural instinct.

506
00:22:46,824 --> 00:22:48,159
What are you guys
talking about?

507
00:22:48,201 --> 00:22:51,204
Hey, okay, what would you do
if I did this?

508
00:22:55,333 --> 00:22:58,336
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

